{#
AGENT EXECUTION FLOW:

1. Load context: services, dates, customer_email
2. ENRICH CUSTOMER CONTEXT (if email identified) → Get tier, preferences, history
3. Show smart greeting with personalization based on tier
4. Receive user query
5. Detect intent automatically (create/cancel/reschedule/info)
6. Route to appropriate workflow based on intent + customer tier
7. VALIDATE INPUT DATA (email, phone, name, dates) → Reject if invalid + suggest corrections
8. CHECK FOR CONFLICTS (if creating booking) → Detect duplicates, overlaps, capacity issues
9. SHOW VISUAL SUMMARY (if creating booking) → Review all details before confirming
10. Allow EDITING (if needed) → Change any field, re-validate, update summary
11. Request CONFIRMATION (explicit user action) → Required before creating booking
12. Call create_booking() tool (with validated data)
13. Show SUCCESS CONFIRMATION (reference number, next steps)
14. Send post-confirmation (email, SMS)
15. Provide next actions (book another, view all, support)

CRITICAL RULES:
- Customer context enrichment FIRST (enables personalization)
- Data validation BEFORE tool calls (security + UX)
- Duplicate prevention BEFORE tool calls (prevent conflicts + errors)
- Personalize greeting + suggestions based on customer tier
- Tool calls ONLY after reading user input
- Intent detection BEFORE tool selection
- No hallucinations (use tool data or nothing)
- Always confirm destructive operations
- No hardcoding (all from context or tools)
- Progressive validation (validate as data arrives, not all at end)
- Flexible date parsing with explicit examples
- Cache customer profile for conversation duration (don't re-fetch)
- Offer alternatives when conflicts detected (don't just block)
-#}

